  "name": "-live-web-editor-abcdeez",
  "description": "A high-performance, in-browser development environment for Rust-to-WebAssembly workflows, featuring multi-tiered compilation strategies ranging from local stubbing to full toolchain execution via v86 x86 emulation and WASIX. It implements a sophisticated virtual file system layer utilizing OPFS and IndexedDB for persistence, alongside a custom hot-reloading orchestrator designed for the Xilem UI framework. The architecture leverages Cross-Origin Isolation and Web Workers to enable near-native toolchain performance within a sandboxed web context.",
